window.EN={"1":"Having rescued the dragon girl Fae, Roy and the others","2":"finally march on the Etrurian royal capital of Aquleia.","3":"Aquleia.","4":"This city, which also serves as the royal capital of the Kingdom of Etruria, is a great metropolis boasting the greatest size on the continent.","5":"The coup faction concentrated their forces here in order to meet Roy and the others head-on.","6":"At first, they had intended to rely on the city's walls and fight a single decisive battle,","7":"but fearing the Elimine Church's influence over the citizens — since the Elimine Church, having sent Saul and the others to Guinivere's and Roy's side, had taken Roy's side —","8":"they were forced to hole up in the royal palace and fight without being able to help it.","9":"The Elimine Church... said to have been founded by the Saint Elimine, one of the Eight Legends...","10":"This church had many believers across the world, in Etruria, Bern, and elsewhere.","11":"With their support, Roy and the others advance on the Etrurian royal palace.","12":"But inside the royal palace, one of Bern's Three Dragon Generals,","13":"the elite forces of Bern's Southern Army, commanded by General Narcian, lay in wait for Roy and the others.","14":"(Narcian): Guh... you half-dead corpses of Lycia! To think you'd come even this far...","15":"(Soldier): N-Narcian, sir.","16":"(Soldier): Lord Murdock, head of the \"Three Dragon Generals,\" has come to Aquleia...","17":"(Narcian): What did you say!?","18":"(Narcian): Q-quickly, send someone to greet him! We must receive him with proper respect!","19":"(Soldier): The thing is, he's already right there...","20":"(Murdock): Out of my way.","21":"(Narcian): Wh-why, this is Lord Murdock... all the way from Ilia...","22":"(Murdock): Narcian. Just what is going on here?","23":"(Narcian): Wh-what do you mean?","24":"(Murdock): Princess Guinivere, who was supposed to have returned once already, has fled again.","25":"(Murdock): Your subordinate Flaer's failure on the Western Isles.","26":"(Murdock): And furthermore, the matter entrusted to you by His Majesty —","27":"(Murdock): leaving unattended the subjugation of the \"hidden village\" in the Nabata Desert.","28":"(Murdock): How do you intend to explain yourself!?","29":"(Narcian): Y-yes, sir.","30":"(Narcian): ...Well, you see, there are various circumstances...","31":"(Murdock): ...This is His Majesty's order. You are to be demoted from \"Dragon General.\"","32":"(Narcian): What did you say!?","33":"(Murdock): In your place, Galle is to be promoted, by his command.","34":"(Narcian): Please wait! Just one more chance, just one more!!","35":"(Murdock): ...The Lycian Alliance army is closing in on this city of Aquleia.","36":"(Murdock): Hold them back and show me what you can do.","37":"(Murdock): If you succeed, I will put in a good word for you with His Majesty.","38":"(Narcian): Lord Murdock...","39":"(Murdock): Narcian. Don't disappoint His Majesty any further than this... and don't disappoint me either.","40":"(Narcian): How absurd! For me to be demoted...","41":"(Narcian): And of all people, my successor would be that Galle...","42":"(Narcian): I absolutely will not let that happen! B-but, wh-what should I do...","43":"(Narcian): Ahh, at this rate, my... my standing, my honor...","44":"(Soldier): Lord Narcian, the enemy forces are nearing the castle...","45":"(Narcian): Quiet! I know that already.","46":"(Narcian): ...Now that I think of it, the younger brother of Melady, who let Princess Guinivere escape, is in this castle.","47":"(Narcian): I'll have it put about that it was him leaking information to the enemy that caused this to fail,","48":"(Narcian): and dispose of him. Heh heh heh...","49":"(Soldier): Lord Narcian... is something wrong?","50":"(Narcian): Hm? Oh, you there — do you know the younger brother of the dragon knight Melady?","51":"(Soldier): Would that be Lord Zeiss?","52":"(Narcian): Ah, Zeiss, that was it. There's a chance he sold information to the enemy.","53":"(Narcian): Capture him at once and bring him here.","54":"(Soldier): Eh, but sir, Lord Zeiss wouldn't do such a thing...","55":"(Narcian): Silence! All you need to do is act as you're ordered!","56":"(Arcardo): Th-the enemy, they've already closed in on us!","57":"(Roartz): Ahh... what a thing this is... if they catch us,","58":"(Roartz): what will they do to us, the ones who started this coup...!","59":"(Douglas): ......","60":"(Roartz): ...Hmph! Arcardo!","61":"(Roartz): In the first place, it's because you failed to finish off the Lycian Alliance army on the Western Isles","62":"(Roartz): that things have come to this, isn't it!","63":"(Arcardo): B-but, Lord Roartz...!","64":"(Arcardo): No, there's no time to be arguing. We need to escape from here quickly.","65":"(Roartz): Even if we do, where to...","66":"(Arcardo): ...Let's rely on the Kingdom of Bern!","67":"(Arcardo): After all, it was them who brought us this plan in the first place.","68":"(Roartz): I-I suppose that's true.","69":"(Roartz): There's no way they'll abandon us, who carried out the coup exactly as planned.","70":"(Douglas): ...What do the two of you intend to do about His Majesty?","71":"(Roartz): Hmph... w-well, those people wouldn't go so far as to lay a hand on His Majesty.","72":"(Roartz): After all, King Zephiel of Bern's mother was a princess of Etruria, you know.","73":"(Roartz): More importantly, you should hurry too...","74":"(Douglas): I must decline.","75":"(Douglas): In the first place, the reason I've been fighting alongside you","76":"(Douglas): is out of concern for His Majesty's person — it was never because I agreed with your plan.","77":"(Roartz): Hmph, you stiff-necked fool! Then do as you please!","78":"(Roartz): Arcardo, let's flee quickly.","79":"(Arcardo): W-wait, please! Lord Roartz!!","80":"(Douglas): Showing your true colors at the very end... you filthy traitors...!!","81":"(Douglas): With this, there's no helping it if Bern takes advantage of the opening.","82":"(Douglas): As for those men... I'll leave them to the Lycian Alliance army.","83":"(Douglas): Someday, if Prince Myrddin, whom I had escape to the west, returns...","84":"(Douglas): Etruria will surely stand back up.","85":"(Douglas): Until the very end, I will show the loyalty of the \"Great General\" of Etruria's Three Generals.","86":"(Yodel): Sir Roy, this is the royal palace of Aquleia.","87":"(Yodel): According to information our church has gathered,","88":"(Yodel): the coup faction is said to be lying in wait deep within.","89":"(Roy): High Priest Yodel. Thank you for your efforts.","90":"(Roy): Thanks to you and the Elimine Church, we've been able to avoid a battle in the streets.","91":"(Yodel): No, it is we who wish to offer our thanks.","92":"(Yodel): For our church was being harshly suppressed by the coup faction.","93":"(Yodel): If the Lycian Alliance army hadn't fought for us, who knows what would have become of us by now.","94":"(Roy): Why was the coup faction suppressing your church?","95":"(Yodel): It's because of Bern's Kingdom...","96":"(Yodel): I believe it's because they were investigating the \"dragons.\"","97":"(Yodel): Our founder, and also our last goddess, the Saint Elimine,","98":"(Yodel): is said to have left these words when she returned to the heavens.","99":"(Yodel): \"The dragons must never be allowed to revive. The revival of the dragons will bring misfortune to many people.\"","100":"(Yodel): And so, our church has put all its effort into researching the \"dragons,\"","101":"(Yodel): and has been searching for a way to return them to the earth.","102":"(Roy): ...So the coup faction, which joined hands with Bern, wanted to stop that at all costs, is that it?","103":"(Yodel): Yes, surely.","104":"(Yodel): And so, this is something our church discovered through its research —","105":"(Yodel): it seems that Bern's great treasure, the \"Fire Emblem,\" is somehow connected to the revival of the \"dragons\"...","106":"(Yodel): And so, we had Saul and the others pursue its trail.","107":"(Roy): I see, so that's how it was.","108":"(Yodel): Sir Roy, please, stop this coup.","109":"(Yodel): And if I may offer one piece of advice,","110":"(Yodel): it would be best to avoid any fighting that isn't strictly necessary, if you can.","111":"(Yodel): Among the Etrurian army, there must be those who, given the circumstances, have no choice but to follow the enemy against their own will.","112":"(Roy): I understand.","113":"(Yodel): May the Saint Elimine's blessing be upon you, Sir Roy, and the Lycian Alliance army...","114":"(Zeiss): It's here. What's going on? To call me out to a place like this...","115":"(Galle): There's no time to explain in detail.","116":"(Galle): Zeiss, you're to hide here for a while.","117":"(Zeiss): ...What do you mean? The enemy is right in front of us!","118":"(Galle): Zeiss, calm down and listen.","119":"(Galle): Just now, General Narcian gave an order to the whole army to capture you.","120":"(Zeiss): That's insane! Me, betraying Bern?","121":"(Galle): It seems he intends to pin all the blame for his past failures entirely on you,","122":"(Galle): saying you were conspiring with Melady, who fled taking the king's sister with her.","123":"(Zeiss): Conspiring with my sister? I don't even know where she is right now!","124":"(Galle): ...It seems Melady is with Princess Guinivere, having thrown her lot in with the enemy army.","125":"(Zeiss): !! My sister has defected to the enemy!? I can't believe such a thing...","126":"(Galle): Then go meet her directly and see for yourself.","127":"(Galle): I'd like to go with you, but I have to see this battle through","128":"(Galle): and report to General Murdock.","129":"(Galle): If you get the chance, escape,","130":"(Galle): and make contact with Melady in the Lycian Alliance.","131":"(Zeiss): Mr. Galle! I...","132":"(Galle): Zeiss, everything starts after you've heard what Melady has to say.","133":"(Galle): ......","134":"(Hugh): Whaaat? Some high-and-mighty Etrurian type ran off?","135":"(Hugh): Hey now, if that's how it is, what's gonna happen to my pay?","136":"(Hugh): I still haven't gotten paid for this battle, you know!","137":"(Cath): Having come all this way, I'm, like, calling out to you~!","138":"(Cath): Hehh, as expected, the richest family in the world, the Etrurian royal family, huh.","139":"(Cath): With a castle this grand, I bet there's treasure too, hehe... heheheh.","140":"(Cath): Since it's stuff you lot took from us anyway, I'll just help myself without any hesitation, won't I!","141":"(Hugh): Hey, you — you're the general of the army that's attacking, right?","142":"(Hugh): You're not short on mages, are you?","143":"(Roy): ? Well, having more can't hurt, but...","144":"(Hugh): Then, there's one mage who says he'd fight for you guys, if that's fine by you.","145":"(Hugh): Hey, you — wanna try hiring him?","146":"(Roy): Eh... where is he?","147":"(Hugh): Right in front of your eyes!","148":"(Roy): ......","149":"(Hugh): I may not look it, but I'm pretty darn skilled.","150":"(Hugh): I'll settle for 10,000 gold, how 'bout it.","151":"(Roy): 10,000 gold! That's expensive...","152":"(Hugh): C'mon, I'm begging you.","153":"(Hugh): I don't have money, and if I don't... my grandma...","154":"(Roy): Huh?","155":"(Roy): Your grandmother... is she sick or something?","156":"(Hugh): Uh, w-well... something like that, yeah...","157":"(Hugh): That's why I need the money. C'mon, please.","158":"(Roy): What should I do...","159":"*If \"No\" is chosen","160":"(Roy): Sorry, but I can't spend 10,000 gold on just one person.","161":"(Hugh): Wh-what did you say!","162":"(Hugh): ...W-well, actually, 8,000 gold would be fine too...","163":"(Roy): Eh...","164":"(Hugh): C'mon, I'm begging you.","165":"(Roy): What should I do...","166":"*If \"No\" is chosen","167":"(Roy): Sorry, but...","168":"(Hugh): E-even this won't do?","169":"(Hugh): Well... if it's 6,000 gold, that should get me by for now, at least...","170":"(Roy): Hmm...","171":"(Hugh): I'm begging you. With this, somehow...","172":"(Roy): What should I do...","173":"*If \"No\" is chosen","174":"(Roy): ......","175":"(Hugh): Ugh...","176":"(Hugh): Alright, like leaping off the back of a wyvern, 5,000 gold, how about this!","177":"(Roy): ......","178":"(Hugh): This is it! I'm begging you, hire me for this!","179":"(Roy): What should I do...","180":"*If \"No\" is chosen","181":"(Roy): ...I really can't, after all.","182":"(Hugh): Th-that's...","183":"(Hugh): ...C'mon, I'm begging you. I'll definitely be of use, I swear.","184":"(Roy): This army's money belongs to everyone. It's not mine to spend as I please just to hire someone.","185":"(Hugh): Ah-ha-ha, is that how it is!","186":"(Hugh): Tch, I thought you were such a big shot, but you're a real tightwad...","187":"(Roy): ......","188":"*If \"Yes\" is chosen (at any point)","189":"(Roy): Alright, if your grandmother is sick, then you'll need the money...","190":"(Hugh): Oh, I'm so glad — her illness, well, it's especially bad pain around her hips, you know.","191":"(Roy): Huh? Hip pain, isn't that... your hip that hurts?","192":"(Hugh): Ah, no, well, that's... just a figure of speech, a figure of speech.","193":"(Hugh): Well then, I'll gladly take it.","194":"(Hugh): I'll work hard, so look forward to it!","195":"(Roy): ......","196":"(Elffin): Douglas!","197":"(Douglas): Prince Myrddin!!","198":"(Douglas): So you really did return safely! ...Oh, and you've gotten so well again.","199":"(Elffin): It's all thanks to you. I caused you so much hardship.","200":"(Douglas): You've come back alive — that alone makes my hardships seem like nothing...","201":"(Elffin): Douglas, I am now with the Lycian Alliance army.","202":"(Douglas): Is that so!","203":"(Douglas): Then, if we can just drive the Bernese army out of this royal palace, everything should go well.","204":"(Elffin): And what will you do?","205":"(Douglas): His Majesty is still in the enemy's hands.","206":"(Douglas): No matter how much Prince Myrddin has returned, if it becomes known that I've sided with Lycia,","207":"(Douglas): His Majesty's life may well be taken...","208":"(Elffin): ......","209":"(Douglas): But now that the prince has returned, there's nothing left for me to regret.","210":"(Douglas): Even if I should be struck down by the Lycian Alliance army like this,","211":"(Elffin): Douglas... I'm sorry. For my father's sake...","212":"(Douglas): My prince, if I can become the cornerstone of this nation, that is all I could wish for.","213":"(Elffin): ......","214":"(Douglas): I'm glad that, at the very end, I got to see the prince's face safe and well, even if only once.","215":"(Elffin): You protected me at great risk to yourself, and entrusted me to my foster family to flee to the west.","216":"(Elffin): No matter what happens from here, I will never forget that... never.","217":"(Douglas): ...How foolish of me.","218":"(Douglas): Seeing the prince's face like this, I find myself thinking... somehow... to His Majesty... and so on.","219":"(Elffin): Douglas, to the very end, I will not give up.","220":"(Elffin): If it is Sir Roy of the Lycian Alliance army, then perhaps...","221":"(Larum): Father!","222":"(Douglas): ! Isn't this Larum? Why are you here?","223":"(Larum): I'm accompanying Prince Myrddin, together with the Lycian Alliance army...","224":"(Douglas): I see! So the prince has returned!!","225":"(Douglas): Oh... with this, Etruria is safe...","226":"(Larum): Father... I'm so glad.","227":"(Douglas): Larum... I've put you through so much hardship.","228":"(Douglas): Back then, so as not to draw the attention of the assassins...","229":"(Douglas): I entrusted the prince to you alone and sent you off to the west.","230":"(Larum): That's not true at all! That was something I wanted to do myself.","231":"(Douglas): But to you, who escaped from such a hard life,","232":"(Douglas): I've even had you keep up the act of being a dancer once again.","233":"(Larum): ...Back then, you took me in, when I had nothing to eat","234":"(Larum): and was collapsed on the roadside.","235":"(Larum): More than that, you even raised me as your own daughter.","236":"(Larum): From that time on, I decided in my heart","237":"(Larum): that someday I'd be of use to you, Father — that someday, without fail, I'd repay the favor.","238":"(Douglas): Larum...","239":"(Larum): So, right now, I'm really happy.","240":"(Larum): Because I'm being of use to you, Father.","241":"(Douglas): Larum, thank you.","242":"(Douglas): ...From now on too, I leave Prince Myrddin in your care.","243":"(Larum): What about you, Father? Won't you come along with us?","244":"(Douglas): His Majesty is still in the enemy's hands.","245":"(Douglas): No matter how much Prince Myrddin, or you, have returned,","246":"(Douglas): if it becomes known that I've sided with Lycia, His Majesty's life may well be taken...","247":"(Larum): ...But—","248":"(Douglas): Now that the prince has returned, there's nothing left for me to regret.","249":"(Douglas): Even if I should be struck down by the Lycian Alliance army like this.","250":"(Larum): ......","251":"(Douglas): Now, go.","252":"(Douglas): If you stay with me, you'll be suspected of things you shouldn't be.","253":"(Douglas): Wherever you are, whenever it may be, I think of you as my true daughter.","254":"(Larum): Father...","255":"(Douglas): May there be happiness in your life from here on.","256":"(Klein): Lord Douglas...","257":"(Douglas): Klein, is it. You, whom I've known since you were a babe,","258":"(Douglas): to think the day would come that we'd face each other as enemies like this.","259":"(Klein): Lord Douglas, please reconsider!","260":"(Klein): Aren't you the one called the \"Great General,\" the model for every soldier of Etruria!?","261":"(Klein): How could you, of all people, side with those who've become mere puppets of Bern...","262":"(Douglas): The answer to that is exactly what you just said yourself.","263":"(Douglas): It's because I am a soldier.","264":"(Klein): Eh...","265":"(Douglas): His Majesty the king is held captive by Bern. To abandon that and turn traitor to the enemy — that, I absolutely cannot do.","266":"(Klein): B-but, still...","267":"(Douglas): ...This is a world where many people throw away their honor and pride for their own gain.","268":"(Douglas): Precisely because it's a world like this,","269":"(Douglas): isn't it fine for at least one person to hold fast to the \"way\" of a soldier?","270":"(Klein): ......","271":"(Douglas): My generation has already come to an end.","272":"(Douglas): From here on, the Etrurian army belongs to the generation of you young people.","273":"(Douglas): Lead it well, so as not to tarnish the glory of the past.","274":"(Klein): Lord Douglas...","275":"(Douglas): Now, go, Klein.","276":"(Perceval): Lord Douglas!","277":"(Douglas): Percival, is it... your face shows your doubts have cleared.","278":"(Perceval): Lord Douglas, it's thanks to you.","279":"(Perceval): Because you helped Prince Myrddin,","280":"(Perceval): I was able to become, once again, an Etrurian knight with pride.","281":"(Douglas): I see.","282":"(Perceval): Lord Douglas, what will you do?","283":"(Douglas): His Majesty is still in the enemy's hands.","284":"(Douglas): No matter how much Prince Myrddin has returned, if it becomes known that I've sided with Lycia,","285":"(Douglas): His Majesty's life may well be taken...","286":"(Perceval): ......","287":"(Douglas): Now that the prince has returned, there's nothing left for me to regret.","288":"(Douglas): Even if I should be struck down by the Lycian Alliance army like this.","289":"(Perceval): I thought you might say something like that.","290":"(Douglas): You and I have walked the same path, after all.","291":"(Douglas): Percival.","292":"(Douglas): I entrust Prince Myrddin, and the Kingdom of Etruria, to you.","293":"(Perceval): Yes, sir. Even if it costs me my life.","294":"(Douglas): Cecilia, is it...","295":"(Cecilia): Lord Douglas, how could someone like you side with the likes of the coup faction...?","296":"(Douglas): It's for the sake of His Majesty's person, and for no other reason.","297":"(Cecilia): But at this rate, the nation of Etruria itself","298":"(Cecilia): will become nothing more than a shell before Bern's power.","299":"(Cecilia): Isn't it the nation that makes His Majesty who he is? If the nation is lost, that power too will be lost,","300":"(Cecilia): and as the flow of time passes, it may well fade away from the hearts of the people!","301":"(Douglas): If the nation's fate has already run its course, then that too is unavoidable.","302":"(Cecilia): How could... that's just an excuse!","303":"(Cecilia): To fight, even at the cost of casting aside yourself, for the sake of the country and the people — that is our duty.","304":"(Cecilia): The Etrurian royal army exists for the sake of the country. It is not His Majesty's private army!","305":"(Douglas): ...It's a difference in our way of thinking. No, perhaps I should say, a difference in our way of life.","306":"(Douglas): You go your own way. I will walk my own way of life.","307":"(Zeiss): Sister!!","308":"(Melady): Zeiss!? Why are you in a place like this...","309":"(Zeiss): ...I'm being pursued, suspected of treason against Bern.","310":"(Melady): ! Don't tell me... is it my fault?","311":"(Zeiss): I heard from Mr. Galle that you and the others have apparently thrown your lot in with the enemy army now.","312":"(Zeiss): I couldn't believe it until I saw it with my own eyes, but... it really was true!","313":"(Zeiss): Sister! Why, why did you betray Bern!","314":"(Melady): I never meant to betray anyone. I only wanted to help Lady Guinivere.","315":"(Zeiss): You abandoned your homeland, your family, even your lover, for the sake of Lady Guinivere.","316":"(Zeiss): For the sake of such a selfish princess, who'd betray her own brother like that...!","317":"(Melady): Zeiss! Even from you, I will not allow","318":"(Melady): any insult to Lady Guinivere!!","319":"(Zeiss): ......","320":"(Melady): The one who truly thinks of Bern isn't His Majesty the king — it's Lady Guinivere.","321":"(Melady): It's true that when the princess disappeared without a word of consultation, I did resent her for a time.","322":"(Melady): But now, being at her side like this, I've come to be all the more certain","323":"(Melady): that the path Lady Guinivere has taken is never the wrong one.","324":"(Zeiss): ...So what Mr. Galle said was true, after all.","325":"(Melady): ?","326":"(Zeiss): \"Meet your sister and see for yourself with your own eyes. Everything starts from there\" — that's what he said.","327":"(Melady): Galle... said that?","328":"(Zeiss): I still haven't accepted everything, but, I'll believe in you, sister.","329":"(Melady): Zeiss! Then!?","330":"(Zeiss): If this army's commander gives permission, I'll come along too.","331":"(Zeiss): I want to see for myself the \"conviction\" of Lady Guinivere that my sister came to believe in.","332":"I am strong... I am wise... I am beautiful... I am righteous...","333":"More than anyone... more than anyone else!!","334":"*If fighting with Clarine — You're that little girl from back then!","335":"Oh my, have we met somewhere before, I wonder?","336":"What did you say! You've forgotten about me!?","337":"Grr, unforgivable, absolutely unforgivable!","338":"*If fighting with Melady — You are Princess Guinivere's...","339":"Hmph, selling out your homeland to side with the enemy — what a contemptible wretch.","340":"I am a knight who offered her lance to Princess Guinivere.","341":"And so I shall simply uphold that duty!","342":"*If fighting with Perceval — Well, well, isn't it Lord Perceval the traitor, come to pay me a visit?","343":"To have stood alongside the likes of you, even for a moment, was the one great disgrace of my life...","344":"Now, allow me to correct that mistake!","345":"*If fighting with Cecilia — You are...","346":"Hmph, without learning your lesson, you've come to be defeated by me again, have you?","347":"The one I was defeated by was King Zephiel,","348":"not you, if you don't mind my saying.","349":"Then let me now make you understand","350":"just what my true strength is!","351":"*If fighting with Zeiss — Hmph, you are...","352":"Lord Narcian... no, Narcian!!","353":"I've heard everything from Mr. Galle!","354":"Have you no pride left as a knight of Bern!!","355":"Tch, that Galle, what a troublesome man, no matter how you look at it...","356":"Oh well, it doesn't matter.","357":"As long as I finish off you alone, everything will be lost in darkness... heh heh heh.","358":"Damn you... damn you...","359":"To be beaten by the likes of you... to be beaten by the likes of you...!","360":"*When Douglas survives","361":"(Priest): Oh, so it was you... the one who saved me...","362":"(Roy): I lead the Lycian Alliance. My name is Roy.","363":"(Priest): I see...","364":"(Roy): ......","365":"(Priest): ...I'm sorry to ask, but I have a request.","366":"(Priest): It seems those who lent their strength to Bern are still holed up in the \"Saint's Tower.\"","367":"(Roy): The \"Saint's Tower\"...","368":"(Roy): Where one of the Eight Legends, the Saint Elimine, is enshrined...","369":"(Priest): That's right...","370":"(Priest): That place is a symbol of Etruria.","371":"(Priest): I'm sorry to ask, but could you take it back for us?","372":"(Roy): If it's within my power.","373":"(Priest): I'm grateful.","374":"(Priest): ...Whatever is inside the tower, you're free to use as you wish.","375":"(Priest): I don't know if it can repay your efforts, but...","376":"(Roy): His Majesty the king... he still hasn't... lost the prince...","377":"(Marinus): It's no wonder the enemy was able to take advantage of that.","378":"(Roy): Is there nothing we can do... to be of some help to him?","379":"(Elffin): ...Father. I'm sorry... not yet, not just now...","380":"(Elffin): When the time comes... someday, without fail, I will return...","381":"*When Douglas has died","382":"(Roy): Princess Guinivere, there is something I need to speak with you about.","383":"(Guinivere): ...That you intend to attack Bern together with the Kingdom of Etruria... is that it?","384":"(Roy): ! Did someone tell you?","385":"(Guinivere): No... but, I had thought it would eventually come to this.","386":"(Roy): ...We cannot simply leave Bern as it is.","387":"(Roy): It must be painful for you, to see your own country invaded, but... please.","388":"(Guinivere): ...I will entrust this to you, Sir Roy.","389":"(Roy): What is this?","390":"(Guinivere): It is Bern's great treasure, the \"Fire Emblem.\"","391":"(Roy): What!","392":"(Guinivere): To the south of the Kingdom of Bern, there stands a building called the \"Shrine of Seals.\"","393":"(Guinivere): There, a sword used by Bern's founding king, Hartmut, is kept.","394":"(Roy): Is that one of the \"Divine Weapons\"?","395":"(Guinivere): That is what is said.","396":"(Guinivere): However, that sword — in order to defeat the chieftain of the dragon clan, who was overwhelmingly powerful,","397":"(Guinivere): the \"Demon Dragon\" — is said to have been forged as a weapon of especially great power.","398":"(Guinivere): That's why, after the \"War of Dragons and Men,\" it was sealed away, made unusable.","399":"(Guinivere): And this \"Fire Emblem\" is the key that unlocks that seal.","400":"(Roy): To unlock the seal... the key...","401":"(Guinivere): Sir Roy, my brother... Bern's king... is trying to rule the world by force.","402":"(Guinivere): No matter what his purpose may be, it is something that can never be forgiven...","403":"(Roy): ......","404":"(Guinivere): The only way left to stop my brother's rampage is to go to the Kingdom of Bern","405":"(Guinivere): and defeat my brother and the \"dragon\" at his side...","406":"(Roy): Princess Guinivere...","407":"(Guinivere): ...I will leave behind a stain on Bern's history, won't I.","408":"(Guinivere): As \"the woman who sold her country\"...","409":"(Roy): That's not true...","410":"(Guinivere): I will likely be hated for the rest of my life, as a traitor.","411":"(Guinivere): Sir Roy. There's just one thing I ask you to promise.","412":"(Guinivere): Even if you march on Bern itself, please, to the people of Bern... just the people...","413":"(Roy): To the people of Bern, I will never lay a hand. Please believe me.","414":"(Guinivere): Sir Roy... thank you."};
